Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome back to curious archive  this video is the second half of my  two-part series on the biology of  horizon zero dawn  in the most extreme biomes of this world  of machines ill-tempered titans  skilled survivalists and genuine terrors  still await discovery like the animals  braving the harshest regions of our  current age these machines have had to  get creative to endure the hazards of  the elements  the environments are perilous in the  machines that live here even more so but  sometimes discovery requires certain  risks  and with mysterious robots that aren't  part of the ecosystem awakening in the  darkest corners of the land who knows  what final secrets are buried beneath  the ground  so join me on the last section of our  documentary style journey as we conclude  our expedition across the uncharted  regions  in the dense jungles of the far south a  fearsome storm batters the trees  typically i'd wait until such weather  passes but right now time is of the  essence for one of the rarest and most  spectacular machines of all has been  spotted here  a huge shadow passes overhead  above my position is the single  mightiest machine of all the skies  a storm bird  they're huge with wing beats so powerful  they echo like thunderclaps the storm  bird is not afraid of the hurricane  raging around them for this machine is  the storm  and unfortunately for me these solitary  beings are highly territorial soaring  close to the ground the storm bird  crackles with electrical discharge  at the heart of this machine is what  appears to be an electric field  generator and this storm bird is about  to give me a zap  my camera takes the brunt of the blast  this is why you always bring extra  recording equipment documenting a storm  bird in the middle of a storm turns out  to be an inadvisable idea  eventually however the storm calms down  and after losing sight of me the  stormbird has also mellowed out in the  warm light of dawn it is easier to  appreciate the majesty of this ruler of  the skies across the land there are no  machines quite like them and our  sighting is a promising start to the  expedition  without the gloom of the storm the true  beauty of this jungle emerges with just  the right amount of sunlight and  nutrients this tropical band of forest  is a paradise yet even the luscious  gardens have their thorns  a chill runs down the back of my neck a  shimmer seems to ripple in the morning  light  i don't think i'm alone  something invisible is moving through  the underbrush  for a brief moment the camouflage  flickers  and the stealthy machine becomes  perceptible  this is a stalker a nimble hunter whose  sinewy frame seems designed in every way  for ambush attacks their demeanor  mirrors that of a large feline predator  with each measured step hiding the  incredible speed they're truly capable  of and the stalker can take their  ambushes to another level through the  use of optical camouflage they can  project the terrain behind them onto  their bodies this form of invisibility  is almost perfect with only a slight  bend in the light suggesting the  stalkers outline  and as the stalker moves they leave  behind small proximity mines that will  detonate if i get too close  alerting the stalker to my presence  trying to keep one eye where i'm  stepping and one eye on the underbrush  is harrowing yet i have discovered a  single weakness in order to take in  light the stalker's optical sensors must  remain visible if i keep watch for these  floating dots i should be able to  anticipate attacks  yet knowing an attack is coming is one  thing surviving an attack is another one  stalker has evidently decided they've  waited enough and goes on the offensive  uncloaking they take a hurried swipe at  my head  a close call  every part of the stalker is built for  combat from the metal claws and teeth of  their front to the stinger-like blade at  the end of their tail i doubt this is a  fight i can win  yet just as quickly as the stalker  appears they vanish  disappearing once more to wait for their  next opportunity i'm not keen on another  surprise attack and decide to continue  my expedition in a region with a thinner  underbrush  i travel to the north a region where  very little vegetation grows  here a vast stone quarry stretches along  the length of a canyon this colossal  excavation project appears long  abandoned yet somehow the site still  feels occupied a terrible rumbling  echoes through the quarry  something is moving under the surface of  the rock  for a brief moment a gigantic machine  breaches from the sand like a surfacing  whale stumbling backwards i witnessed  the metal goliath rise up and clamp  their jaws where i had just been  standing  before diving once again  that was a rock breaker one of the  largest known machines these agents of  destruction can shred through any  material like a sentient excavation  drill they use this ability to swim  under the earth's crust as a fish moves  through water when they detect a sound  they move shark-like to the source of  the noise and attack the unlucky target  from below if a target is difficult to  apprehend rock breakers will briefly  surface  giving us a chance to look more closely  at their anatomy while they might  function like a fish rock breakers  possess powerful limbs that resemble an  excavator shovel tunneling animals like  badgers or moles have similar digging  mitts that they use to create their  burrows  the most prominent tunneling tool of the  rock breaker though is their massive  mouth composed of an enormous roller  cone drill bit with this feature a rock  breaker can swallow vast quantities of  raw material each day yet what goes down  must come up and the rock breaker needs  to regularly regurgitate processed  stones into the air which rain down upon  the surface  with a rock breaker on the loose this  quarry is as perilous as it gets  time to tiptoe away to our next location  in the western desert i spot a herd of  antelope-like creatures racing over the  dunes these are lance horns and while i  only catch a glimpse of them they look  majestic yet they are clearly in a hurry  and i soon find out why out of nowhere a  heavy sandstorm sweeps over the western  reaches  stumbling through the storm i find  various familiar machines are also  struggling to press on against the  howling winds all any of us can do is  keep moving and hope the storm dies down  but there is something in this cloud  more dangerous than the elements  stalking within the sandstorm is a  terror from a lost age  moving on four scorpion-like legs this  machine isn't like the others i've seen  not a part of the larger machine  ecosystem they possess no behavior  beyond unreasoning hostility  yet how did such a machine come to be  this stretch of desert called the rust  watch is scattered with mysterious ruins  it seems a battle was waged here long  ago with many dormant machines of war  now rusting away in the sand  perhaps this corruptor is the last one  still functioning a thoughtless agent of  war from a conflict that ended a  millennia ago  in any case i have a more current  problem the corrupter has spotted me yet  to my surprise before the corrupter can  strike other machines descend upon it  from all directions unleashing every  attack in their arsenal like immune  system cells descending upon an  infection the other machines seem to  instinctually see the corrupter as a  threat to the ecosystem it's a  surprising turn but not one i wish to  dwell on as the ensuing chaos has given  me the perfect opportunity to make a  hasty exit yet while i leave the rust  watch i can't help but wonder if there  are other long lost machines hidden away  in the margins of this world  with the western desert and southern  jungle now charted the greatest frontier  of all still remains far to the north  the frozen wilds in immense mountainous  region beckoned with the promise of  untouched wilderness temperatures drop  low in the forests and mountains of  these wilds with the wind carrying cold  drafts of snow between the trees it's a  good thing i've come with layers yet  some denizens of this mountainous forest  don't have to bundle up rushing ahead of  me is a herd of remarkable machines  chargers  these swift-footed beings are the  champions of the freezing alpine slopes  and are comfortable on inclines most  creatures wouldn't dare to climb  in behavior and general appearance  chargers are perhaps most similar to  mountain goats  there are organic mountain goats present  in this region in a rare instance of  machines alongside the animal whose role  they fill as herbivorous machines  chargers spend much of their time  seeking out patches of vegetation  unlike some herbivores though chargers  have an aggressive side when i step too  close the machines rush towards me  kicking wildly to scare me off i  certainly now understand why these  animals are called chargers it's a  lesson i'll be sure to remember better  leave these slopes to the chargers  moving to the valley below i discover a  landscape of surreal prismatic hot  springs these natural springs exist in  the modern day and tells me this is a  region we would know as yellowstone  national park the bright vivid colors in  the spring are the result of microbial  mats around the edges of the  mineral-rich water  and dropping at the water's edge is a  herd of bellowing giants these huge  stocky machines are known as tramplers  with their massive head neck and chest  tramplers look like no force on earth  could knock them down with so much bulk  they seem to be less bothered by the  falling temperatures than i am like the  bison of north america tramplers are  highly resistant to the wind and snow  and for any non-elemental challenges a  pair of huge horn-like structures keep  the tramplers prepared for anything  tramplers also use these horns to dig up  rock and soil they work tirelessly  stopping only to change location to  another spot but for what purpose soil  analysis suggests that tramplers are in  fact purifying the toxin-laden soil of  this land  they filter the material they dig up  through a processing unit on their  underside which glows with heat from its  arduous task  with each region the tramplers pass  through the immediate ecosystem becomes  a little healthier but tramplers aren't  always peaceful highly territorial these  bulls will charge interlopers with  unpredictable speed  if pushed tramplers will even use their  processing units to set the environment  ablaze scorching the land they typically  protect  wanting to avoid such an outcome i stay  out of range of the herd's optical  sensors and watch them pass  on cresting the next hill i witness a  tall neck trudging through the snow it's  surprising to see one this far north but  it seems not even the cold can slow  these beings down or the trees for that  matter which this tallneck seems to take  little notice of i find it is comforting  to see a familiar machine in such an  unfamiliar land yet just ahead looms a  machine that is distinctly unfamiliar  these are control towers and unlike all  other types of machines they look  botanical rather than zoological to my  astonishment the strange machine then  releases a cloud of spiraling drones  into the air  that burst with bizarre purple energy as  it turns out control towers act as the  unofficial hearts of the synthetic  ecosystem with their drones helping to  repair nearby machines their bizarre  appearance is the result of this  peculiar sessile lifestyle why bother  with locomotion when your legion of  loyal drones can go anywhere you can't  while the undulating movements of these  towers subtly resemble the motion of  coral control towers have no clear  natural analogs yet in repairing damaged  machines the importance of their role in  the continued health of the ecosystem  cannot be overstated and with such a  vital occupation control towers are  fiercely defended by the machines they  repair  on that note i think i've gotten close  enough already  to the north the snowfall has become  heavier like the sandstorm in the  western desert a blizzard descends over  this region in a matter of minutes even  with my layers of protection i'll need  to find shelter if i am to survive this  onslaught in the distance i spot a cave  illuminated with the artificial lights  of the hunter-gatherer communities who  occupy this region perhaps refuge awaits  inside  no such luck  from the cave emerges a fiery machine  this is a scorcher and they have taken  over this cave from its previous  occupants their tall pointed ears give  them a vulpine appearance although  scorchers seem far less skittish i  suspect the snow is now the least of my  worries  waiting for an attack i watch the  scorcher crouch down then rock it  forwards leaving a blazing trail a near  hit  despite living in a cold environment the  scorcher is an agent of the inferno  creating devastating if somewhat  inaccurate walls of fire i might be cold  but this is no way to warm up  time to find a different shelter  stumbling through the storm i happen at  last upon a snow-covered ruin the  structure has seen better days but i'll  have to take my chances  the inside is thankfully much warmer but  what is this a ruin of  a collection of forgotten animal statues  in the corner gives me a clue i'm  standing in the ruins of the yellowstone  national park visitor center and these  statues are sadly the last record of  their respective species once this  building falls these animals will be  lost to time  through a crack in the wall i noticed  the snow outside has calmed down  the time has come to complete the final  leg of my journey  at the foot of the mountains rises a  fortress like ruin this was once a  hydroelectric dam through which vast  quantities of water still flow and  stalking the base of this dam is one of  the most dangerous machines of the  frozen wilds a frost claw  like polar bears frost claws have  muscular builds and are practically  immune to the cold  indeed frost claws are the champions of  the ice  using a chemical similar to liquid  nitrogen frost claws can create sharp  spikes of frozen coolant transforming  the surrounding area into a forest of  jagged ice  much of the dam is now covered with  these glacial stalagmites  and this frost claw is not alone a fire  claw has also made their home on this  dam  this infernal machine is even larger  than their icy cousin and they are known  to be even more aggressive the frost  claws opposite fire claws wield flames  much like scorchers frost and fire claws  might not seem like they'd get along but  surprisingly these two seem to tolerate  each other with both a frost claw and a  fire claw at this site close  documentation is a serious risk  fortunately the dam's ruins provide  reliable cover  all i have to do is find a space too  narrow for the machines to fit through  and stay hidden until the coast is clear  at the very edge of the world the final  stop on our journey is a bleak graveyard  like the wreckage of the rust watch this  seems to have been the site of a great  battle yet who or what were the ancient  humans fighting against when  civilization fell  tromping through the snow is a metal  monster unlike any seen before this  ancient horror is a deathbringer the  last machine standing in this grim  cemetery like the smaller corruptor i  encountered in the sands the  deathbringer has no resemblance to any  fauna and is simply a unit of  destruction many of its weapon systems  are no longer functioning but it seethes  with blind hate nonetheless  perhaps it was rogue units like this one  that were the cause of humanity's  collapse or perhaps the deathbringers  were aided by something much bigger  throughout my travels i've witnessed  many immense metal tentacles snaking  over the mountains these machines known  simply as metal devils have been in the  back of my mind this entire voyage  no still functioning units of this  machine are known to exist but their  proximity to ruined battlefields raised  suspicion i suspect these machines were  responsible for the doom of the previous  ecosystem and the animal machines that  populate this land were built to return  the world to a habitable state  in time these ruins will hopefully be  forgotten  and earth will become the planet it once  was  warming up in the temperate safety of  the embrace i consider all i've seen in  this strange future while a quiet  sadness permeates throughout the ruins  of this world the interconnected  machines that populate the land have  given the planet new life so to speak  i've heard rumors of a vastly different  ecosystem of machines in a region known  as the forbidden west and if passage to  that location is ever possible perhaps  someday i'll chart it as well but for  now the time has come to return home  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious see you in  the next video  you

